using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace CompetitiveRounds
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Embedded machine-draft catalogues (localization-design D4: drafts
    /// render LIVE and count 0% toward the reviewed metric; a language with
    /// no moderator yet is still fully usable). Keys are the exact English
    /// source strings the chokepoints see; values preserve the source's TMP
    /// tag sequence VERBATIM (I18n.RegisterCatalogue rejects any entry whose
    /// tag order differs — the §2.5 injection guard).
    ///
    /// Glossary (locked, never translated): Ranked, FFA, 1v1/1v2/2v2, Elo,
    /// RLFP, Discord, Steam, DLL, PNG, FPS, mode/room names.
    ///
    /// Four locales (es, ru, uk, sv), each covering the full extracted
    /// source registry (tools/i18n_source.json; see I18nSourceKeys.g.cs).
    /// Entries are agent-authored machine drafts validated against the
    /// mirrored server rules before commit (learning #298e). es/ru carry a
    /// few extra keys retired by later English edits — harmless, and kept
    /// so a rollback of that edit still finds its translation.
    /// </summary>
    internal static class I18nCatalogues
    {
        public static void Install()
        {
            I18n.RegisterCatalogue("es", ES);
            I18n.RegisterCatalogue("ru", RU);
            I18n.RegisterCatalogue("uk", UK);
            I18n.RegisterCatalogue("sv", SV);
        }

